# Task 146-001: Agent Truncation Bug Fix — Execution Plan

## Root Cause
`src/orchestra/task-builder.ts:761` — `agentPrompt.slice(0, 2000)` truncates agent prompt to 2000 chars.
Typical agent PROMPT.md is 3000-5000+ chars, causing mid-sentence cut like "Clean up fil".

## Fix
1. Remove `agentPrompt.slice(0, 2000)` limit in `buildWorkerPrompt()` — use full agent prompt
2. Note: `resolveAgentPrompt()` in result-collector.ts already loads PROMPT.md fully — no change needed there
3. agent-pool.ts has NO truncation — it only manages agent.json files, not PROMPT.md content

## Files to Modify
- `src/orchestra/task-builder.ts` — Remove .slice(0, 2000) from agentPrompt (line 761)

## Files to Test
- `tests/core/agent-pool.test.ts` — Add 5 tests verifying no truncation in prompt pipeline

## Test Plan
1. loadAgent('architect') returns full PROMPT.md content (>1000 lines mock)
2. loadAgent('test-writer') returns full content
3. loadAgent('doc-writer') returns full content
4. Cache invalidate returns fresh full content
5. buildWorkerPrompt() output does not contain "Clean up fil" truncation
